MiniMax-H3 video engine (h3), vendored

Source: the h3 engine repository, branch main, commit
8c4a054674787175d293232dbc0c884eceb9cad4 ("DEVELOPMENT.md"). Plain copy, without
its git history.

What came from where:

  h3 runtime/engine/*                 -> runtime/video/engine/
  h3 runtime/model/*                  -> runtime/video/model/
  h3 runtime/ops/*                    -> runtime/video/ops/
  h3 runtime/metal/MetalBackend.*     -> runtime/video/metal/
  h3 include/h3/h3.h (C ABI)          -> runtime/video/abi/h3.h
  h3 runtime/metal/abi/*              -> runtime/metal/abi/video/
  h3 runtime/metal/kernels/common/*   -> runtime/metal/kernels/video/common/
  h3 runtime/metal/kernels/GROUP/F    -> runtime/metal/kernels/video/GROUP_F
                                         (GROUP: dit, vae, preview; shared/F -> F)

The only edits are the include paths, rewritten for these locations
("engine/" -> "video/engine/", "model/" -> "video/model/", "ops/" -> "video/ops/",
"metal/MetalBackend.hpp" -> "video/metal/MetalBackend.hpp", "metal/abi/" ->
"metal/abi/video/", "metal/kernels/common/" -> "metal/kernels/video/common/",
"h3/h3.h" -> "video/abi/h3.h"). Code and kernel arithmetic are unchanged.

One local patch, to send upstream: WeightStream.mm creates each slot's
`free` semaphore at 0 and signals it once instead of creating it at 1.
libdispatch traps (SIGTRAP, "Semaphore object deallocated while in use")
when a semaphore is disposed below its creation value, which a slot the SSD
reader holds is when the DiT is released after a streamed run.

Splash's own files beside the vendored tree: VideoJob.{hpp,mm} (the
`splash video-native` process the server runs per job) and this note.

Build: the kernels compile with Splash's production Metal flags into
splash.metallib (the video kernel group), the host code with Splash's flags
plus -ffp-contract=off, as h3 builds it, into build/engine/libsplash-video.a.
With these flags the 3 s golden request's final latents, video VAE frames and
TAEH3 preview frames are byte-identical to h3's references (dev/tests/video).

